-- `l4 batch` re-prints the module and runs the printed text. A newline inside a
-- string used to be printed raw, so it became a layout line break that took the
-- body's indentation, and batch answered "line\n  next" where `l4 run` answers
-- "line\nnext", with status success (smucclaw/l4-ide#1028).

@export default the text
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE s x IS
    IF x > 0
    THEN "line\nnext"
    ELSE "tab\there"

#EVAL s 1
#EVAL s 0
